CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 44 slow path via lambda: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 46 fast path via lambda: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
A `[&]` lambda inside a member function template calls a sibling
member function TEMPLATE of the enclosing class unqualified, expanding
the enclosing function's parameter pack (libc++ vector::emplace_back's
__if_likely_else fast/slow-path lambdas).  Per N5008
[class.mfct.non.static]/3 the call is `(*this).slow_path(...)` on the
ENCLOSING object, which the capture-default captures
([expr.prim.lambda.capture]/8).  Previously the member template was
not recognised as a member of the enclosing class, the closure's own
`this` was used, and the lambda bodies were silently dropped.
